  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Justice in Climate Policy (2024), published by Springer Nature, has been cited 7 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 231 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Justice in Climate Policy by Annick de Vries, Gijsbert Werner, Elsenoor Wijlhuizen and others was published by Springer Nature in 2024. It is part of the Research for policy series. Conceptually, the work connects to Economic Justice, Climate justice, Political science, Sociology and Criminology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 7 citations. Citations peaked in 2026 with 4 citing works. Notable citing venues include Sustainability, Policy Studies and Wiley Interdisciplinary Reviews Climate Change. The citing works include 6 journal articles and 1 book chapter. They come from 7 countries, led by the Netherlands, China and Spain.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 231 times via OAPEN. Open Library reports a combined count of 1 reading logs and catalog editions.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\" data-wiki-books=\"verified\">The latest English Wikipedia check verified 1 article–work reference matches. These are references or bibliography entries, which may include other editions of the same work; they do not measure readership.</p>\n",
